00:22:25.574 --> 00:22:27.033
So just live your life…

00:22:28.368 --> 00:22:29.619
and come over on vacation.

00:22:31.079 --> 00:22:32.831
I'd forgotten.

00:22:32.914 --> 00:22:36.042
You're a guest, so you can come anytime.

00:22:38.003 --> 00:22:40.630
This summer doesn't have to be the last.

00:22:41.965 --> 00:22:44.634
Just go ahead
and do that Hermann project.

00:22:46.178 --> 00:22:48.013
Once you're done, come visit.

00:22:48.096 --> 00:22:49.097
Hey, Song Ha-gyeong.

00:22:49.181 --> 00:22:51.141
Then I'll take a day off to hang with you.

00:22:52.517 --> 00:22:54.477
You know I'm a pro at hosting guests.

00:23:13.914 --> 00:23:15.498
Bullshit.

00:23:23.673 --> 00:23:25.342
Gosh, this is bullshit.

00:23:31.139 --> 00:23:34.351
I'm not saying this to you.
It's this summer I'm talking about.

00:23:36.519 --> 00:23:38.772
What? Come visit?

00:23:39.689 --> 00:23:42.108
Host me as a guest? Unbelievable.

00:23:47.989 --> 00:23:49.282
What brings you here?

00:23:52.327 --> 00:23:54.788
Yang Jae-ho. Pacheon-si, Gyeonggi-do.

00:23:54.871 --> 00:23:56.915
-Patan-myeon, Nakham-ri 12, right?
-Yes.

00:23:56.998 --> 00:23:58.124
All right, three sacks.

00:23:58.750 --> 00:23:59.626
Three sacks.

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.297
-Three sacks.
-Two sacks.

00:24:04.381 --> 00:24:07.926
-Two sacks.
-Being young is great.

00:24:08.051 --> 00:24:09.928
By the way, why do you look like that?

00:24:10.011 --> 00:24:11.137
What do you mean?

00:24:12.931 --> 00:24:14.349
What, do I look like a guest?

00:24:14.975 --> 00:24:15.934
Here.

00:24:17.477 --> 00:24:18.395
Good.

00:24:19.354 --> 00:24:21.648
Next, Nam Jeong-su.

00:24:21.731 --> 00:24:22.816
Five sacks.

00:24:24.567 --> 00:24:26.611
Look at you, so strong!

00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:42.419
How come you're so weak?

00:24:42.502 --> 00:24:44.963
You're way taller than me.
I'm disappointed.

00:24:45.046 --> 00:24:47.924
It's because your push is off balance!

00:24:48.008 --> 00:24:50.302
It feels like
I'm the only one pushing here.

00:24:50.385 --> 00:24:52.679
This has got to move.

00:24:55.098 --> 00:24:57.976
The parking brake!
That's why it's stuck!

00:24:58.059 --> 00:25:00.854
-But I checked.
-What do you think you're doing?

00:25:00.937 --> 00:25:02.480
Hey, Jin-guk.

00:25:03.106 --> 00:25:04.858
You got a new car? Move it now.

00:25:05.483 --> 00:25:08.653
You can't just park here.

00:25:08.737 --> 00:25:11.072
The fence is already high,
blocking the view.

00:25:11.156 --> 00:25:13.074
-Wait, who are you?
-Me?

00:25:15.535 --> 00:25:17.245
I live here.

00:25:17.871 --> 00:25:18.997
I'm a resident here!

00:25:29.174 --> 00:25:31.217
Ha-gyeong?

00:25:43.063 --> 00:25:45.523
Su-bak.

00:25:46.274 --> 00:25:47.817
Have you eaten?

00:25:49.319 --> 00:25:51.780
For Patan to become a better town,

00:25:51.863 --> 00:25:53.406
it needs development.

00:25:53.490 --> 00:25:57.535
So should we focus
on expanding roads or fixing drainage?

00:25:57.619 --> 00:26:01.456
Ladies and gentlemen,
why don't we vote with a show of hands?

00:26:01.539 --> 00:26:03.124
I think streetlights

00:26:03.208 --> 00:26:05.168
are more urgent than that,
don't you think?

00:26:07.670 --> 00:26:09.130
And who are you?

00:26:09.214 --> 00:26:11.216
Me?

00:26:11.299 --> 00:26:15.261
I'm the resident of Peanut House,
Patan-myeon, Jangsu-ro 101-23.

00:26:17.222 --> 00:26:20.809
And speaking of the bus number 18,
it takes forever to come,

00:26:20.892 --> 00:26:22.352
but it barely even stops.

00:26:23.019 --> 00:26:24.687
And water deer, right?

00:26:24.771 --> 00:26:26.398
The reward should go up.

00:26:26.481 --> 00:26:28.733
Considering the crop
and residential damage,

00:26:28.817 --> 00:26:30.318
the estimated damage is--

00:26:31.778 --> 00:26:36.116
Wait, Mr. Architect.
How long have you lived in Patan, again?

00:26:37.200 --> 00:26:40.370
It's been 22 days.

00:26:41.913 --> 00:26:45.250
He's a real piece of work,
worse than Dr. Song.

00:26:49.504 --> 00:26:52.048
No one measures up to Dr. Song,

00:26:52.132 --> 00:26:54.843
but Director Baek,
I'll make you a master.

00:26:54.926 --> 00:26:57.011
How's that sound, "Master Baek"?

00:26:57.095 --> 00:26:59.431
You're not at Dr. Song level,

00:26:59.514 --> 00:27:01.850
but a bachelor's feels too low.

00:27:01.933 --> 00:27:03.601
"Master" is just right for you.

00:27:03.685 --> 00:27:05.645
After trying it myself,

00:27:05.728 --> 00:27:09.190
I realized Ha-gyeong
definitely earned that Dr. Song title.

00:27:09.315 --> 00:27:12.610
Of course. When it rains,
she's the one checking for leaks.

00:27:12.694 --> 00:27:14.946
When it snows, she's the one

00:27:15.029 --> 00:27:19.409
pestering the township head
to get sand and calcium chloride.

00:27:19.492 --> 00:27:22.745
She even replaced the bus stop benches

00:27:22.829 --> 00:27:25.623
with ones that have
both heating and cooling.

00:27:26.166 --> 00:27:28.334
There's no one like Dr. Song.

00:27:28.418 --> 00:27:30.211
Master Baek, you can't keep up.

00:27:35.884 --> 00:27:38.303
No, that's not it.

00:27:38.803 --> 00:27:42.265
This will kill the persimmon tree
at the persimmon lady's house.

00:27:42.807 --> 00:27:46.102
Her dried persimmons are always a must
at the women's events.

00:27:46.728 --> 00:27:48.396
It's the township office's fault.

00:27:48.480 --> 00:27:50.190
Why should the residents suffer?

00:27:50.273 --> 00:27:53.193
Treat the tree right now!

00:27:56.613 --> 00:27:59.657
Ma'am, you didn't dress warm enough.

00:27:59.741 --> 00:28:00.950
I'm cold.

00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:05.371
In weather like this, it's dangerous
to be alone. You could get hurt.

00:28:05.455 --> 00:28:06.998
Thanks, Ha-gyeong.

00:28:08.124 --> 00:28:09.125
Here.

00:28:09.209 --> 00:28:11.836
Keep yourself warm.
It's too cold for your bones.

00:28:18.968 --> 00:28:19.886
What?

00:28:40.865 --> 00:28:42.492
I'm Master Baek now.

00:28:43.827 --> 00:28:45.703
They can't call me "Dr. Baek" yet.

00:28:46.246 --> 00:28:48.122
But at least I got the master's.

00:28:51.668 --> 00:28:53.086
Do I still feel like a guest?

00:28:58.091 --> 00:28:58.925
Song Ha-gyeong.

00:29:00.802 --> 00:29:02.720
Your plan's just too obvious.

00:29:04.222 --> 00:29:06.391
You treat me like I'm not even here.

00:29:06.891 --> 00:29:08.768
You come home late on purpose.

00:29:09.602 --> 00:29:12.522
And like you said,
you make me feel like I don't belong,

00:29:12.605 --> 00:29:14.607
leaving me hanging, till I finally leave.

00:29:15.567 --> 00:29:19.404
You're making me realize
how lonely this house is, so I'll leave.

00:29:20.488 --> 00:29:22.615
You think I don't see what you're doing?

00:29:23.575 --> 00:29:25.243
If you know, just leave, okay?

00:29:28.121 --> 00:29:29.455
Number one, my foot.

00:29:35.837 --> 00:29:37.213
Just wait for me in the summer.

00:29:38.464 --> 00:29:41.301
Summer is in both our names.

00:29:42.802 --> 00:29:44.220
That's so childish.

00:29:46.389 --> 00:29:48.808
Fine. Whatever.

00:29:49.475 --> 00:29:52.395
For summer, I'll make you my number one.

00:29:53.146 --> 00:29:53.980
Happy?

00:29:56.399 --> 00:29:58.526
You said I'd be number one in summer,

00:30:00.361 --> 00:30:02.405
that you'd only think of me.

00:30:20.381 --> 00:30:21.382
You must be hungry.

00:30:22.842 --> 00:30:24.636
I feel bad making you do all the cooking.

00:30:25.595 --> 00:30:28.598
You must be exhausted from working
in the sun all day, right?

00:30:28.681 --> 00:30:29.891
What are you doing?

00:30:30.516 --> 00:30:33.561
My mom said a good host
treats guests well,

00:30:34.187 --> 00:30:36.606
making sure they leave
without feeling disappointed.

00:30:38.524 --> 00:30:39.359
Go ahead, eat.

00:30:41.319 --> 00:30:42.695
Are you joking?

00:30:42.779 --> 00:30:44.238
No need to do the dishes.

00:30:44.322 --> 00:30:46.616
Why are you acting nice?
That's not like you.

00:30:46.699 --> 00:30:48.618
-You're upset because I'm being nice?
-Yes.

00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:51.996
Don't be nice. Yell at me to get lost,

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:55.124
get mad, throw a fit, and just be mean!

00:30:55.667 --> 00:30:57.669
Why would you act all nice?
It's so annoying.

00:31:26.447 --> 00:31:28.908
What? Was it today already?

00:31:30.451 --> 00:31:32.036
Time really flies.

00:31:37.125 --> 00:31:38.418
I loved summer.

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:42.130
Or rather, I had to love it.

00:31:44.257 --> 00:31:46.175
I had waited for the summer

00:31:47.301 --> 00:31:48.845
through the endless cold.

00:31:56.853 --> 00:31:59.105
I was convinced that summer was mine.

00:32:00.773 --> 00:32:01.607
But then…

00:32:03.568 --> 00:32:06.446
you ended up disappearing from the summer.

00:32:08.031 --> 00:32:09.991
I let my guard down because it was summer.

00:32:11.659 --> 00:32:13.286
I thought summer was mine…

00:32:15.496 --> 00:32:17.206
or at least that's what I believed.

00:32:25.298 --> 00:32:27.300
For summer, I'll make you my number one.

00:32:32.013 --> 00:32:34.098
I'll wait only for you,
at least in summer.

00:32:48.988 --> 00:32:52.950
Hi, Hyun.
Sorry for calling so late.

00:32:53.951 --> 00:32:56.913
I have a favor to ask.

00:33:10.802 --> 00:33:12.804
The date on your ticket was yesterday.

00:33:13.513 --> 00:33:14.889
So it's already past, right?

00:33:16.808 --> 00:33:18.810
You wanted Do-ha return
to where he should be.

00:33:20.770 --> 00:33:25.108
I know I don't have the power
or position for that,

00:33:25.191 --> 00:33:27.068
but I'm doing my best.

00:33:28.861 --> 00:33:31.030
Why haven't you
managed to bring him back yet?

00:33:32.949 --> 00:33:35.910
You came in so strong,
but your skills seem to fall a bit short.

00:33:41.958 --> 00:33:42.792
I'll admit that.

00:33:43.876 --> 00:33:46.671
I didn't know much
about Do-ha here in Pacheon.

00:33:49.799 --> 00:33:51.467
I don't really know him either…

00:33:52.844 --> 00:33:54.095
these days.

00:33:54.762 --> 00:33:56.013
Ms. Song.

00:33:57.265 --> 00:34:00.184
Did you know the first step in remodeling
is always demolition?

00:34:00.768 --> 00:34:04.021
To fix anything,
you first have to know what needs fixing

00:34:04.105 --> 00:34:05.982
and start by tearing it down.

00:34:07.275 --> 00:34:10.611
Whether it's nostalgia,
illusions, delusion…

00:34:12.029 --> 00:34:12.864
or old memories.

00:34:13.489 --> 00:34:14.991
Whatever it is.

00:34:16.284 --> 00:34:18.161
But Do-ha isn't doing that.

00:34:20.705 --> 00:34:24.167
Do you know why?

00:34:28.838 --> 00:34:30.173
How am I supposed to know…

00:34:31.382 --> 00:34:32.633
the reason?

00:34:37.555 --> 00:34:40.474
Thank you for completing the revisions
on a tight schedule.

00:34:41.142 --> 00:34:43.269
The team leader
will now handle supervision.

00:34:45.438 --> 00:34:47.857
I'll stay involved in carrying out
the design intent.

00:34:49.525 --> 00:34:51.277
Design continues through construction.

00:34:52.361 --> 00:34:53.487
Sure.

00:35:01.621 --> 00:35:04.624
Letting Director Jeon go
turned out to be great.

00:35:05.333 --> 00:35:08.502
Sure, we had to do all the hard work,
but the site's organized.

00:35:08.586 --> 00:35:12.173
And with the updated plans,
we got a new inspection and safety rating.

00:35:12.757 --> 00:35:16.052
Ms. Jeon hasn't complained either.
Isn't that great?

00:35:18.721 --> 00:35:20.223
It is great.

00:35:20.306 --> 00:35:23.142
Everything's going smoothly.
There's nothing to worry about.

00:35:23.226 --> 00:35:24.560
But you seem so unmotivated.

00:35:26.854 --> 00:35:29.440
Can you check the pipe connections?
I'm leaving now.

00:35:30.149 --> 00:35:30.983
What?

00:35:31.692 --> 00:35:33.945
-Thanks.
-Sure.

00:35:34.028 --> 00:35:37.323
Why did you ask me
to introduce you to Su-hyeok?

00:35:37.949 --> 00:35:41.702
I don't know.
I brought this on myself.

00:35:43.079 --> 00:35:45.706
Seung-taek, I've become Master Baek.

00:35:46.791 --> 00:35:48.209
Master Baek?

00:35:48.292 --> 00:35:50.419
Ha-gyeong completely disappeared

00:35:51.671 --> 00:35:53.256
from the Peanut House and Pacheon.

00:35:54.048 --> 00:35:56.759
-What?
-She's all work, and so am I.

00:35:56.842 --> 00:35:58.177
Song's out on dates.

00:36:01.931 --> 00:36:02.932
What?

00:36:04.475 --> 00:36:05.810
With her boyfriend.

00:36:07.103 --> 00:36:11.065
You're the one who missed your chance.
Su-hyeok grabbed his.

00:36:12.108 --> 00:36:13.901
Hey, Seul…

00:36:13.985 --> 00:36:15.736
-Whose side are you on?
-Song's side.

00:36:16.445 --> 00:36:19.407
You've spent nearly 20 years
without defining a relationship,

00:36:19.991 --> 00:36:23.035
but Su-hyeok went for it right away!

00:36:24.745 --> 00:36:25.997
Come on, Seul.

00:36:32.503 --> 00:36:34.463
Was I too harsh earlier?

00:36:34.547 --> 00:36:37.174
No, he has to learn his lesson.

00:36:39.635 --> 00:36:40.594
Seung-taek.

00:36:43.681 --> 00:36:45.850
Should we go to Patan for our anniversary?

00:36:46.475 --> 00:36:47.893
To see the Summer Triangle?

00:37:10.916 --> 00:37:12.168
You didn't forget, right?

00:37:12.918 --> 00:37:14.045
How could I forget?

00:37:14.628 --> 00:37:17.048
I was annoyed
you were always looking down on me.

00:37:17.673 --> 00:37:18.799
Now I'm paying you back.

00:37:19.425 --> 00:37:21.927
How does it feel looking up at me?

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:24.180
Beautiful.

00:37:30.436 --> 00:37:32.897
PACHEON CITY HALL

00:37:37.068 --> 00:37:39.779
Ms. Song, isn't this the place
where we caught

00:37:41.113 --> 00:37:43.199
those high school kids
when we were on duty?

00:37:44.784 --> 00:37:45.743
You're right.

00:37:46.369 --> 00:37:49.372
Now that Patan High is being remodeled
into an observatory,

00:37:49.455 --> 00:37:51.040
high schoolers are saying

00:37:51.123 --> 00:37:53.918
the magic of confession day
will disappear.

00:37:54.001 --> 00:37:55.753
Apparently, the one who started it

00:37:55.836 --> 00:37:59.048
said it must happen
on Patan High's rooftop.

00:37:59.924 --> 00:38:03.552
I heard from Officer Pi
that they're increasing patrols.

00:38:04.095 --> 00:38:07.848
What if the kids rush in again
and cause trouble?

00:38:11.227 --> 00:38:12.436
July 7.

00:38:32.998 --> 00:38:34.291
What was that?

00:38:54.061 --> 00:38:58.023
Hey, Song. You know the photo
from the July 7th stargazing,

00:38:58.858 --> 00:39:01.569
the one in the box?

00:39:02.445 --> 00:39:03.779
Can you give it to me?

00:39:06.282 --> 00:39:10.077
I wanted to share it with Seung-taek
on our 12-year anniversary.

00:39:10.161 --> 00:39:12.413
-Sure, I'll look for it.
-Song.

00:39:13.038 --> 00:39:16.834
I'm sorry
if I brought up any painful memories.

00:39:16.917 --> 00:39:20.504
Hey, don't make a big deal.
It's just a photo.

00:39:22.339 --> 00:39:24.842
Right, you two were inseparable
since then.

00:39:26.802 --> 00:39:28.220
I'll look for it.

00:40:11.597 --> 00:40:13.974
See? My Himalayan climbing tip.

00:40:14.058 --> 00:40:17.478
You have to eat dāl bhāt
with your hands, okay?

00:40:17.561 --> 00:40:18.812
Okay, I get it.

00:40:20.189 --> 00:40:21.023
Hey.

00:40:22.149 --> 00:40:23.567
Are you leaving soon?

00:40:25.027 --> 00:40:26.070
I have to.

00:40:26.612 --> 00:40:28.614
To see Do-ha before I leave,

00:40:28.697 --> 00:40:30.491
I'd better keep myself busy.

00:40:36.747 --> 00:40:37.581
Are you…

00:40:39.333 --> 00:40:40.292
not talking to Do-ha?

00:40:42.878 --> 00:40:45.297
He won't need me
when you take such good care of him.

00:40:48.133 --> 00:40:51.637
In any case, tell me more
about that dāl bhāt thing.

00:40:52.221 --> 00:40:55.808
So, it's basically a set meal.

00:40:55.891 --> 00:40:59.520
It's like a local platter, and
it's different depending on the region.

00:41:18.622 --> 00:41:21.250
-Why did you tag along?
-Of course I did.

00:41:21.333 --> 00:41:24.503
Aren't architects supposed to check
their own work?

00:41:25.129 --> 00:41:27.339
You might not know,
but I contributed a lot.

00:41:27.423 --> 00:41:31.010
When you were busy checking the scale
for hours the other day,

00:41:31.093 --> 00:41:32.553
she revised the plans.

00:41:32.636 --> 00:41:34.763
You'd better not say you don't know.

00:41:34.847 --> 00:41:37.808
We've managed to get this far
thanks to PM Yoon

00:41:37.891 --> 00:41:39.435
keeping things moving.

00:41:41.061 --> 00:41:44.148
I want to see the exterior wall texture
and the signpost.

00:41:44.773 --> 00:41:46.942
Knowing you,
it should be freakishly detailed.

00:41:48.027 --> 00:41:50.321
Let's get this done quick
and head back.

00:41:50.404 --> 00:41:52.948
I've got your back, team!

00:41:53.032 --> 00:41:54.617
-Yay!
-Yay!

00:41:55.451 --> 00:41:57.953
-It's off by about 1mm, right?
-Yes.

00:41:58.996 --> 00:42:00.623
-Double-check.
-Okay.

00:42:02.249 --> 00:42:03.542
Everyone, gather around.

00:42:06.795 --> 00:42:10.424
The spacing of these vertical pieces
and the plywood thickness are off by 1mm.

00:42:11.967 --> 00:42:16.096
You said the layout wasn't clear,
so I revised even the detailed plans.

00:42:21.435 --> 00:42:23.145
Park Hyun, what the heck?

00:42:23.228 --> 00:42:24.396
Before you leave,

00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:26.732
please check
the materials and equipment carefully.

00:42:26.815 --> 00:42:28.609
-Are you out of your mind?
-Just in case--

00:42:29.735 --> 00:42:30.569
What's going on?

00:42:31.320 --> 00:42:34.448
You think this is your playground?

00:42:36.367 --> 00:42:38.410
Going up the scaffolding
with no safety gear?

00:42:39.578 --> 00:42:42.164
-You almost fell, you know?
-Come on, Director Baek.

00:42:42.790 --> 00:42:45.501
It was just one story high.
It's fine, isn't it?

00:42:45.584 --> 00:42:48.253
You don't care if he gets hurt
and can never do design work?

00:42:49.755 --> 00:42:51.548
Didn't I tell you to be careful on site?

00:42:52.716 --> 00:42:55.719
If your injury causes delays,
will you take responsibility?

00:42:57.471 --> 00:42:58.347
I'm sorry.

00:42:59.390 --> 00:43:01.433
Hey, what's with him today?

00:43:01.975 --> 00:43:03.769
He's definitely got a temper.

00:43:03.852 --> 00:43:05.729
I've never seen him like that.

00:43:14.947 --> 00:43:16.115
Baek Do-ha.

00:43:17.366 --> 00:43:18.701
Baek Do-ha!

00:43:20.119 --> 00:43:21.412
Don't say anything weird.

00:43:21.495 --> 00:43:23.997
He's in year one,
when accidents happen the most.

00:43:24.081 --> 00:43:26.375
I only talked about basic safety.

00:43:29.878 --> 00:43:32.005
You can go all out with anything on site.

00:43:32.089 --> 00:43:35.217
No, you have to go all out.

00:43:35.300 --> 00:43:37.594
You can never stress safety enough.

00:43:38.095 --> 00:43:40.597
That's all I was talking about.
Don't read more into it.

00:44:04.913 --> 00:44:06.957
Up until three years ago,

00:44:07.040 --> 00:44:09.918
I never thought I'd be able to work
in architecture again.

00:44:11.295 --> 00:44:13.672
I had suffered a serious accident.

00:44:14.923 --> 00:44:16.967
I couldn't even be in tall buildings

00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:19.511
for quite a while.

00:44:20.095 --> 00:44:21.680
I'm not sure if that's why,

00:44:22.389 --> 00:44:25.058
but I ended up moving
to a single-story house.

00:44:26.101 --> 00:44:27.936
I couldn't design anything

00:44:28.020 --> 00:44:30.314
over two stories for quite a while.

00:44:31.315 --> 00:44:32.900
I'd fallen into a slump.

00:44:33.901 --> 00:44:36.111
You can never stress safety enough.

00:44:36.612 --> 00:44:38.071
That's all I was talking about.

00:44:38.697 --> 00:44:39.907
Don't read more into it.

00:44:56.757 --> 00:44:57.841
Hot.

00:44:59.092 --> 00:44:59.927
What are you doing?

00:45:00.636 --> 00:45:01.762
You see,

00:45:01.845 --> 00:45:04.515
the one who recommended this
said I had to eat it this way.

00:45:04.598 --> 00:45:05.766
So hot.

00:45:07.726 --> 00:45:09.228
Who recommended it?

00:45:13.023 --> 00:45:15.150
There was a friend
who loved the mountains.

00:45:15.234 --> 00:45:16.360
He bragged about this.

00:45:17.402 --> 00:45:18.862
This is called dāl bhāt.

00:45:18.946 --> 00:45:22.032
He said this food could make you
succeed in climbing the Himalayas,

00:45:22.115 --> 00:45:22.991
or so he claimed.

00:45:24.117 --> 00:45:25.160
That said,

00:45:25.244 --> 00:45:28.121
he tried climbing the Himalayas
three times after eating this,

00:45:28.205 --> 00:45:29.206
and made it to the top.

00:45:30.666 --> 00:45:33.752
Listening to that story
nearly drove me crazy.

00:45:37.256 --> 00:45:38.465
Is it good?

00:45:41.093 --> 00:45:42.302
What kind of taste is this?

00:45:43.720 --> 00:45:44.555
Try it.

00:45:47.432 --> 00:45:51.812
Anyway, the way he described it

00:45:51.895 --> 00:45:53.981
was way over the top.

00:45:54.606 --> 00:45:57.192
It felt more like a myth
than some superstition.

00:45:58.277 --> 00:46:00.070
But the taste is nothing special.

00:46:00.988 --> 00:46:03.156
I should've tried it sooner
and scolded him.

00:46:05.158 --> 00:46:06.034
Right.

00:46:06.577 --> 00:46:08.996
He's the one who made up
the July 7th superstition.

00:46:09.079 --> 00:46:10.914
It's causing Pacheon a lot of trouble.

00:46:11.999 --> 00:46:15.210
That's why I snuck out today
to have a date with you.

00:46:15.294 --> 00:46:17.087
What's the July 7th superstition?

00:46:18.255 --> 00:46:19.756
It's called Confession Day.

00:46:19.840 --> 00:46:21.925
There's a superstition
that couples who confess

00:46:22.009 --> 00:46:23.343
at Patan High on July 7th

00:46:24.052 --> 00:46:25.012
never break up.

00:46:25.887 --> 00:46:29.057
But since Seul and Seung-taek
are still going strong,

00:46:29.141 --> 00:46:30.934
it might not be just a superstition.

00:46:34.438 --> 00:46:37.441
Had I known about
that superstition earlier,

00:46:38.108 --> 00:46:39.484
I would've confessed today.

00:46:43.071 --> 00:46:46.158
He was seriously good at causing trouble.

00:46:47.492 --> 00:46:51.079
I couldn't help but notice.
It's all in past tense.

00:46:53.248 --> 00:46:54.249
You had a huge fight?

00:46:56.418 --> 00:46:57.794
I wish we had.

00:46:59.838 --> 00:47:01.632
He died three years ago…

00:47:02.633 --> 00:47:03.675
in the mountains.

00:47:07.012 --> 00:47:07.971
I see.

00:47:10.515 --> 00:47:13.602
I was completely honest in front of him.

00:47:16.438 --> 00:47:17.522
And I really regret it.

00:47:20.400 --> 00:47:23.195
Baek Do-ha really gets on my nerves.

00:47:24.529 --> 00:47:26.323
My brother has a knack for it.

00:47:26.948 --> 00:47:27.991
Why is that?

00:47:28.617 --> 00:47:31.787
I feel so comfortable around you.
I can talk about anything.

00:47:33.664 --> 00:47:35.415
But with him, it's always like a war.

00:47:37.459 --> 00:47:38.752
Feeling uneasy for no reason?

00:47:39.878 --> 00:47:43.131
You can't help
but say mean things for no reason?

00:47:43.215 --> 00:47:44.341
Exactly.

00:47:46.385 --> 00:47:47.969
You think that's for no reason?

00:48:04.152 --> 00:48:07.280
Why do I end up saying everything
in front of you?

00:48:09.825 --> 00:48:11.034
That's strange.

00:48:12.536 --> 00:48:14.162
Did something get into the food?

00:48:17.791 --> 00:48:21.545
I talked about Baek Do-young
for the first time in ages.

00:48:23.338 --> 00:48:24.756
And it's to you, Attorney Seo.

00:48:27.759 --> 00:48:30.053
Thanks for sharing it with me.

00:48:32.472 --> 00:48:36.143
By the way,
you're still calling me "Attorney Seo."

00:48:37.894 --> 00:48:39.604
You really don't know what to call me?

00:48:42.482 --> 00:48:43.650
No.

00:48:51.950 --> 00:48:54.870
Then, instead of the name,

00:48:55.495 --> 00:48:57.164
SPEED DIAL 1
ATTORNEY SEO

00:48:57.247 --> 00:48:58.874
I'll be your speed dial number one.

00:49:38.163 --> 00:49:41.333
-Yes.
-Again? Okay, got it.

00:49:41.416 --> 00:49:42.959
I'll sort it out at the site now.

00:49:43.043 --> 00:49:45.253
Sure, I'll send you the documents.

00:49:45.337 --> 00:49:47.255
If they're students, I'll give a warning.

00:49:47.339 --> 00:49:48.173
Bye.

00:49:53.094 --> 00:49:54.471
Sorry I can't take you home.

00:49:54.971 --> 00:49:57.349
No worries. I need to get to the site now.

00:49:57.891 --> 00:50:01.311
Sure enough,
the July 7th thing really happened.

00:50:11.613 --> 00:50:15.075
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
DO NOT ENTER

00:50:20.831 --> 00:50:23.458
CALL

00:50:23.542 --> 00:50:26.628
SONG HA-GYEONG

00:50:36.805 --> 00:50:39.099
Your call has been forwarded
to voicemail…

00:50:50.318 --> 00:50:51.152
SEUL

00:50:57.450 --> 00:50:58.618
I'm busy right now.

00:50:59.953 --> 00:51:02.289
Are you with Ha-gyeong?

00:51:06.835 --> 00:51:08.962
She went to Seoul for a date
with her boyfriend.

00:51:09.045 --> 00:51:10.005
Don't interrupt them.

00:52:29.876 --> 00:52:33.421
Are you doing
first aid yourself right now?

00:52:35.674 --> 00:52:37.384
This is the ER,
with many urgent cases.

00:52:37.968 --> 00:52:39.427
Ms. Song, you need sutures…

00:52:40.428 --> 00:52:44.182
The laceration is clean
and the bleeding's under control.

00:52:44.265 --> 00:52:45.809
Can we just apply Steri-Strips?

00:52:46.726 --> 00:52:47.894
Do you work in this field?

00:52:48.853 --> 00:52:51.856
I dropped out of medical school
in my third year.

00:52:57.195 --> 00:52:58.697
I should've taken you home.

00:52:58.780 --> 00:53:02.659
Gosh, I'm really okay.
This happens a lot.

00:53:02.742 --> 00:53:04.995
When you handle complaints,
this happens often.

00:53:06.204 --> 00:53:07.956
I was shocked when I got the call.

00:53:08.581 --> 00:53:10.542
I'm really fine.

00:53:12.335 --> 00:53:15.922
Still, I'm glad
I set it as speed dial one…

00:53:17.882 --> 00:53:20.260
since Officer Pi contacted me
on speed dial one.

00:53:22.929 --> 00:53:23.847
I know.

00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:26.224
By the way…

00:53:27.892 --> 00:53:30.061
don't we need to let Mr. Baek know?

00:53:31.521 --> 00:53:33.273
What for? I'm okay.

00:53:34.482 --> 00:53:35.900
It's really no biggie.

00:53:36.443 --> 00:53:37.861
And Director Baek

00:53:38.403 --> 00:53:40.864
is sensitive about accidents,
so he'll overreact.

00:53:43.408 --> 00:53:45.535
He'll make a fuss over nothing,

00:53:46.077 --> 00:53:47.871
so don't say anything to him.

00:54:00.341 --> 00:54:02.343
WHERE ARE YOU?
ANSWER THE PHONE.

00:54:02.427 --> 00:54:04.679
HA-GYEONG, WHAT'S UP?
WHY AREN'T YOU COMING HOME?

00:54:07.682 --> 00:54:09.392
SONG HA-GYEONG

00:54:11.394 --> 00:54:13.480
Your call has been forwarded
to voicemail…

00:54:35.293 --> 00:54:36.753
ATTORNEY SEO

00:54:36.836 --> 00:54:37.879
What the…

00:54:43.301 --> 00:54:44.511
Baek Do-ha speaking.

00:54:52.268 --> 00:54:53.103
My goodness.

00:54:54.270 --> 00:54:56.356
I'm not sure if you've heard,

00:54:56.439 --> 00:54:57.941
but Ha-gyeong is in the hospital.

00:54:58.983 --> 00:55:00.985
-Where's the ward?
-That way.

00:55:01.069 --> 00:55:03.154
I'm tied up with work right now.

00:55:03.238 --> 00:55:04.364
Would you mind

00:55:04.447 --> 00:55:07.033
going to the hospital for her
instead of me?

00:55:07.700 --> 00:55:10.954
Because of that July 7th thing,
City Hall was in total chaos.

00:55:11.704 --> 00:55:13.665
Do people have nowhere else to go?

00:55:13.748 --> 00:55:16.126
Why come to an abandoned school to flirt?

00:55:17.127 --> 00:55:21.089
All those young people poured in
and made a complete mess.

00:55:22.799 --> 00:55:24.217
And you ended up getting hurt.

00:55:26.261 --> 00:55:29.472
We might as well make it a holiday
to let them get out of town.

00:55:29.556 --> 00:55:30.723
Aren't you busy?

00:55:40.024 --> 00:55:42.068
How could you not tell me
you had an accident?

00:55:42.819 --> 00:55:44.904
-Because it's nothing.
-Nothing?

00:55:45.780 --> 00:55:47.365
You need two weeks to recover here.

00:55:49.409 --> 00:55:53.288
Song Ha-gyeong, don't you have my number?
Did you delete it?

00:55:53.371 --> 00:55:55.582
Why in the world did you not call me?

00:55:57.876 --> 00:55:58.835
Baek Do-ha.

00:56:00.003 --> 00:56:01.713
Why would I call you?

00:56:01.796 --> 00:56:04.299
-I've got Attorney Seo.
-Hey, Song Ha-gyeong!

00:56:12.765 --> 00:56:14.184
What's with all the drama?

00:56:14.267 --> 00:56:17.395
You were in the hospital and ignored
my calls, and now what?

00:56:18.313 --> 00:56:20.356
"What's with all the drama?"

00:56:22.150 --> 00:56:23.610
Don't you care how worried I am?

00:56:23.693 --> 00:56:27.322
This is why I didn't tell you.
I was going to go home tomorrow anyway.

00:56:27.906 --> 00:56:31.034
It makes me uncomfortable seeing people
popping in over nothing.

00:56:32.327 --> 00:56:35.038
-I'm here just as a formality.
-Why am I the only one?

00:56:35.788 --> 00:56:38.958
Why am I the only one who didn't know,
when everyone else knew?

00:56:46.925 --> 00:56:47.926
Fine, that's enough.

00:56:48.927 --> 00:56:51.971
Everything's sorted out.
It's nothing serious. So just go.

00:56:52.805 --> 00:56:54.224
Are you leaving me out?

00:56:56.434 --> 00:56:58.728
From your daily life and your world?

00:57:03.274 --> 00:57:05.401
Are you doing this
to make me realize that?

00:57:06.027 --> 00:57:07.278
Because I don't get it?

00:57:12.367 --> 00:57:13.576
Hey, Baek Do-ha.

00:57:13.660 --> 00:57:15.745
Looks like you think

00:57:15.828 --> 00:57:18.581
everything I'm doing is just a show
for your sake.

00:57:19.165 --> 00:57:20.500
Please, don't 'cause drama.

00:57:22.085 --> 00:57:25.338
The final argument?
That was two years ago.

00:57:26.256 --> 00:57:27.590
It feels like ages to me.

00:57:28.675 --> 00:57:30.843
I can barely remember
what happened two days ago.

00:57:30.927 --> 00:57:33.388
You're reading too much
into what happened two years ago.

00:57:34.305 --> 00:57:35.557
Isn't that ridiculous?

00:57:36.724 --> 00:57:38.643
I guess you think I meant all that.

00:57:39.269 --> 00:57:42.272
But I just threw in all the random tips
I'd picked up,

00:57:43.064 --> 00:57:45.650
all for the sake of winning the trial.

00:57:46.859 --> 00:57:47.860
Baek Do-ha.

00:57:48.861 --> 00:57:50.071
You know what?

00:57:50.572 --> 00:57:52.115
Whenever you come back,

00:57:52.198 --> 00:57:54.909
all you do is talk about the old me,
who I used to be.

00:58:01.874 --> 00:58:02.875
Song Ha-gyeong.

00:58:03.876 --> 00:58:05.712
You forced me into being a guest…

00:58:07.255 --> 00:58:08.673
and now to be part of the past.

00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.052
Are you panicking
because your box might open?

00:58:45.251 --> 00:58:46.753
-Hi.
-Hi.

00:58:46.836 --> 00:58:48.546
-Ms. Song?
-Yes.

00:58:48.630 --> 00:58:49.881
You can go home today.

00:58:52.300 --> 00:58:55.595
I was worried about an infection,

00:58:55.678 --> 00:58:57.722
but things are going
way better than I expected.

00:58:57.847 --> 00:58:59.932
The first aid was done really well.

00:59:01.392 --> 00:59:03.227
Help her with the discharge process.

00:59:03.311 --> 00:59:04.145
Sure.

00:59:04.228 --> 00:59:05.897
You forced me into being a guest,

00:59:06.731 --> 00:59:08.107
and now to be part of the past.

00:59:08.858 --> 00:59:10.860
Are you panicking
because your box might open?

00:59:11.569 --> 00:59:12.528
I'm sorry,

00:59:13.613 --> 00:59:16.616
but I'd like to stay one more day.
Can I get discharged tomorrow?

00:59:59.701 --> 01:00:01.994
Wait here for a moment. I'll get the car.

01:00:02.662 --> 01:00:03.579
Sure.

01:00:18.928 --> 01:00:19.971
What the heck?

01:00:21.764 --> 01:00:22.598
What are you doing?

01:00:24.726 --> 01:00:26.185
What are you doing?

01:00:48.082 --> 01:00:49.834
Hey, what are you doing?
Stop the car.

01:00:49.917 --> 01:00:51.377
I don't think I'll ever hear

01:00:52.378 --> 01:00:54.797
your true feelings at Patan
or at the Peanut House.

01:00:55.506 --> 01:00:56.507
What?

01:00:57.925 --> 01:00:59.051
Did you buckle up tight?

01:01:01.554 --> 01:01:03.055
We're not going home today.

01:01:45.598 --> 01:01:47.683
Let's stay together tonight, just us.

01:01:47.767 --> 01:01:49.143
This is obsession, okay?

01:01:49.227 --> 01:01:51.521
If you twist it, I will too.
It's us, after all.

01:01:51.604 --> 01:01:53.773
I need to do everything I can too.

01:01:53.856 --> 01:01:55.691
Attorney Seo!

01:01:56.275 --> 01:01:58.110
-Hey, Baek Do-ha.
-Ha-gyeong.

01:01:58.194 --> 01:01:59.946
-Shall we go to Donghae now?
-What?

01:02:00.029 --> 01:02:01.322
Then come over to my place.

01:02:01.405 --> 01:02:02.824
He invited her to his place?

01:02:02.907 --> 01:02:04.242
You haven't eaten yet?

01:02:05.243 --> 01:02:08.538
When it's about Ha-gyeong,
I have no intention of playing fair.

01:02:08.621 --> 01:02:10.581
I blacked out.

01:02:10.665 --> 01:02:13.209
What on earth happened last night?

01:02:13.292 --> 01:02:14.418
Hey, Baek Do-ha.

01:02:14.502 --> 01:02:16.629
Stop! I must be crazy.

01:02:16.712 --> 01:02:18.172
You like someone like her?

01:02:18.256 --> 01:02:20.383
Transparent. Song Ha-gyeong's transparent.

01:02:20.466 --> 01:02:21.759
I've liked you all along.

01:02:21.843 --> 01:02:24.136
I've always liked you, and I still do.

01:02:25.137 --> 01:02:25.972
I like you.